{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Let me sing, pray.</b> Every נא is like עתה." "<b>For my beloved.</b> On account of my beloved, like אמרי לי (Genesis 20:13), on my account." "<b>For his vineyard.</b> On account of his vineyard." "<b>My beloved.</b> Its root is three-letter, and דודי is from the doubled [root]." "<b>On a horn of a son of oil.</b> It was an honored place in the vineyards of Jerusalem. Some say בקרן is in the sense of a high place; בן שמן is from the root of והיה דשן ושמן (Isaiah 30:23), and like לשד השמן (Numbers 11:8), and it is not far-fetched."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:04.807156101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}